Z||000000||maninblack||06-25-2001||09:47 AM||||After I had a local shop replaced my clutch and reseal my leaking headers gasket,I am getting a code 22 and 35.The car was running fine before,idling at a steady 900rpm,now, it idles at 1300rpm and the services engine<BR>lite keeps coming on,what gives ?.All the sensors was only a yr old.<BR>thz in advance||||reg||5
Z||000001||Formula88||06-25-2001||12:40 PM||||Sounds like they knocked some sensors or vacuum lines loose.  Take it back and tell them to fix it.  If you want to be nice, you can tell them the codes you're getting and what they mean.||||reg||11
Z||000002||PBJ||06-25-2001||01:04 PM||||code 22 - throttle position sensor circuit signal voltage is low.<P>code 35 - idle speed error.<P>May have unplugged and left unplugged the throttle position sensor. idle speed error can be caused by vacuum lines off-computer can not restrict air into engine enough to lower idle-it is sucking in air it should not be.||||reg||1
